"{\"url\":\"https://www.microcision.com/copy-of-sales-business-develpment-m\",\"title\":\"BOOKKEEPERS | Microcision\",\"desc\":null,\"og\":null,\"robots\":null,\"imgs\":[\"Microcision logo.png | 31e942_ef154a865afe4fa79723417987ebbaeb~mv2.png\"],\"form\":[],\"iframes\":[],\"sha256\":\"20f7af2af069cb6f47ccf7142fa4ede2f6b9d54553a7a23eadae803b5b508526\",\"text\":\"Skip to Main Content\\n\\nHOME\\n\\nSERVICES\\n\\nABOUT\\n\\nEXPANSION\\n\\nCAREERS\\n\\nCONTACT\\n\\nBOOKKEEPER\\n\\nMicrocision LLC, NJ (On-site)\\n$55,000 \\u2013 $65,000/year\\nFull-time | Monday\\u2013Friday | First shift\\n\\n\\u200b\\n\\nAbout Microcision\\nLocated in a thoroughly modern facility just outside downtown Philadelphia, in Pennsauken, NJ. Microcision is a leader in high precision medical device machining. Life-saving and life-enhancing medical devices are produced and designed every day in our facility.\\n\\n\\u200b\\n\\nRole Overview\\nWe are seeking a detail-oriented and organized Bookkeeper to join our team. Reporting to the Vice President, the Bookkeeper will manage accounts payable/receivable, cash deposits, bank reconciliations, and client finances (for representative payee accounts). This role is essential for maintaining accurate financial records and supporting the overall financial health of the organization\\n\\n\\u200b\\n\\nKey Responsibilities\\n\\nProcess electronic accounts payable and receivable, ensuring timely payments and collections including maintaining a file of each account.\\n\\nPerform account analysis to identify discrepancies and resolve issues promptly.\\n\\nPrepare and post journal entries, including debits and credits, to the general ledger.\\n\\nAssist with audits and financial documentation.\\n\\nMaintain bank accounts and reconciliations.\\n\\nCollaborate with other departments to ensure accurate financial reporting and compliance with Microcision policies.\\n\\nPayroll back up.\\n\\n\\u200b\\n\\nRequirements\\n\\nCollege degree in accounting is preferred\\n\\n5+ years bookkeeping/accounting experience in a manufacturing environment\\n\\nStrong written and verbal communication skills\\n\\nAbility to work independently and use good judgment\\n\\nAbility to commute to Pennsauken, NJ\\n\\n\\u200b\\n\\nBenefits\\n\\n401(k), Health, dental, vision, life insurance, and Paid time off\\n\\n\\u00a9 2022\\u00a0by Microcision LLC\"}"
